as he mentioned several areas saw some  snowfall through the overnight hours  bianca holman stopped by one of those  areas fox hill park on the far west  part of town earlier today to show us  how it was looking out there  we rarely get snow here in the valley so  folks were ready to take advantage of it  here at fox hill park there was a large  crowd  ready to enjoy the snow globe experience  here are some pictures and video from  other parts of town in the northwest  valley there was snow  everywhere coating trees covering the  ground the flurries didn't stop  joggers or early morning commuters from  making their way out  cynthia gainey the organizer of the  vegas strong 5k sent us these pictures  they were taken on the 215 between  cheyenne and lone mountain  she says they got up to three inches of  snow we even got pictures from our  friends in perum  drivers having to clear off their  windshield of snow  before heading off and then our  four-legged friends dogs playing in the  white powder  pam and brett haynes and pahrump sent us  pictures of their dog frank  enjoying the early morning snow it's  been really nice i just like  going down the hills and sledding it's  really cool  i've lived in las vegas my whole life it  doesn't snow here often  that mom and daughter we spoke with were  decked out in their snow gear they said  this was their second time  out to the park on this snow day we know  the snow will be melting  soon but be sure to send us your  pictures and video to our facebook page  instagram and twitter reporting from  summerlin bianca holman 8 news now
 

